ber Optic Pact is the Real Story","src":"Barron's","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMimgFBVV95cUxNTkVRcHZoaVFSeUNSTXVaS3dVQWFRTE4xbWhsaW12T3JYS21uNHJmR3hmZkhtSEJvWEtyYnk2dEw1TUdBTWZUcDB5NVN5VnI4UXBmOWZ1ZU1WSjcwZ0tCbGhGeFJGRDRtYlhCRW9HekNJX1NnNE42cWZNeTZFSWFsQUFpZ3JwQkQ1T3ItZXJNaS1lUk5oXzNkRVdn?oc=5","date":"2026-10-20","zh":"3M 第三季獲利表現穩健，但其亞馬遜光纖協定才是真實的故事"},{"title":"Global flue gas desulfurization market to grow to $31.7B by 2031 amid stricter sulfur emission rules","src":"Pluang","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMikwFBVV95cUxPbE41T1k5Q2Z4QVVCR082TGVCTlJjenhKaFBlSXFuczRrcDRsOHFhY1hVQ29lS1JqTXF1R0FhTkg0eE9VNFhYSkV3OTVKbzRILU9kbzlDUjRKZ3Z6c3pVU3RiVGY1YzliWU1uVTlyNXpjdUptaGV1LXd2MnBBbFdLZVQzeFNvTkRra3VEdDlkTmdxcVE?oc=5","date":"2026-10-20","zh":"隨著硫排放規則更加嚴格，到 2031 年全球煙氣脫硫市場將成長至 $31.7B"},{"title":"Stanley Black & Decker Takes Outdoor Innovation Center Stage at Equip Expo 2026 With DEWALT, Cub Cadet and Hustler","src":"Moomoo","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMisAFBVV95cUxOamgwVExaZUtKbjNnSDUxOFRKVWh6V0ktSjBINmlUR0dOYmw2MnRvSDBKaW42ckllb3M5aUpBUldVeW5RNGtySEZ2S3YybnBRVWVCMDZTSFc0T0xHTGNnaHdnUFFSWXB5MmZTTjI2TkZqNVhkbVgxWVp4UndjVkhaN3NESWd1QmczYjZ1dFoySWlZN1piSk52YUhyUGdJdm04c0xQU3UzUUF2MkF2OXFPeg?oc=5","date":"2026-10-19","zh":"Stanley Black & Decker 攜手 DEWALT、Cub Cadet 和 Hustler 在 2026 年裝備博覽會上佔據戶外創新中心舞台"}],"themes":[{"name":"財報","count":4},{"name":"自駕/機器人","count":1},{"name":"能源/電力","count":1},{"name":"減重藥/生技","count":1}],"biz":{"tenk":{"form":"10-K","date":"2026-02-24","period":"2026-01-03","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/93556/000009355626000009/swk-20260103.htm"},"overview":[{"en":"Stanley Black & Decker, Inc. (\"the Company\") was founded in 1843 by Frederick T. Stanley and incorporated in Connecticut in 1852. In March 2010, the Company completed a merger with The Black & Decker Corporation (\"Black & Decker\"), a company founded by S. Duncan Black and Alonzo G. Decker and incorporated in Maryland in 1910. At that time, the Company changed its name from The Stanley Works to Stanley Black & Decker, Inc. The Company's principal executive office is located at 1000 Stanley Drive, New Britain, Connecticut 06053 and its telephone number is (860) 225-5111.","zh":null},{"en":"The Company is a global provider of hand tools, power tools, outdoor products and related accessories, as well as a leading provider of engineered fastening solutions, with 2025 consolidated annual revenues of $15.1 billion. Approximately 62% of the Company's 2025 revenues were generated in the United States, with the remainder largely from Europe (16%), emerging markets (13%) and Canada (4%).","zh":null},{"en":"In recent years, the Company has re-shaped its portfolio through a series of divestitures. In July 2022, the Company sold its Convergent Security Solutions (\"CSS\") business comprised of the commercial electronic security and healthcare businesses for net proceeds of $3.1 billion and its Mechanical Access Solutions (\"MAS\") business comprised of the automatic doors business for net proceeds of $916 million. In August 2022, the Company sold its Oil & Gas business comprised of the pipeline services and equipment businesses. In April 2024, the Company sold its Infrastructure business, comprised of the attachment and handheld hydraulic tools business, for net proceeds of $729 million. Most recently, the Company announced in December 2025 that it had entered into a definitive agreement to sell its Consolidated Aerospace Manufacturing (\"CAM\") business for $1.8 billion in cash. These divestitures","zh":null}],"markets":[],"customers":[{"en":"A significant portion of the Company's Tools & Outdoor products are sold to home centers and mass merchants in the U.S. and Europe. A consolidation of retailers both in North America and abroad has occurred over time. While this consolidation and the domestic and international expansion of these large retailers have provided the Company with opportunities for growth, the increasing size and importance of individual customers create a certain degree of exposure to potential sales volume loss. The Home Depot accounted for approximately 15% and 14% of the Company's consolidated net sales in 2025 and 2024, respectively, while Lowe's accounted for approximately 12% and 14% of the Company's consolidated net sales in 2025 and 2024, respectively. No other customer exceeded 10% of the Company's consolidated net sales in 2025 or 2024.","zh":null}],"competition":[{"en":"The Company competes on the basis of its reputation for innovation and product quality, its well-known brands, its commitment to customer service, its strong customer relationships, the breadth of its product lines focused on core end-user segments, and customer value propositions.","zh":null},{"en":"The Company encounters active competition in the Tools & Outdoor and Engineered Fastening segments from both larger and smaller companies that offer the same or similar products and services or that produce different products appropriate for the same uses. Certain large customers offer private label brands (\"house brands\") that compete across a wide spectrum of the Company's Tools & Outdoor segment product offerings.","zh":null}],"segments":{"seg":{"end":"2026-01-03","items":[{"name":"Tools & Outdoor","val":13158200000,"zh":"Tools & Outdoor"},{"name":"Engineered Fastening","val":1972200000,"zh":"Engineered Fastening"}],"total":15130400000},"geo":{"end":"2026-01-03","items":[{"name":"US","val":9316800000,"zh":"美國"},{"name":"Europe","val":3079800000,"zh":"歐洲"},{"name":"Asia","val":1213900000,"zh":"Asia"},{"name":"Other Americas","val":839600000,"zh":"Other Americas"},{"name":"CA","val":680300000,"zh":"加拿大"}],"total":15130400000}},"peers":["DOV","PPG","GPC","GWW","VFC"]}}